		(uuid "521e040f-216a-4935-acc6-9ab5a5d0c3b8")
	)
	(text "FPGA5V5 -> DDR_RAW; L1601 + C1604 filter the output.\nVOS and feedback sense RAW before R1605."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22 81.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.15 1.15)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 0 70 190 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "522e4b74-ff54-4d06-beaa-c0f584be64af")
	)
	(text "R1605 (0.01 Ohm) drops 10 mV/A outside feedback. At 3 A, DDR1V35 is about\n1.32 V. R1606 (10 kOhm) bleeds the output. PGR_DDR is open drain, pulled to\nAON by R1602 (10 kOhm); use its RAW status only with FPGA5V5 present. The IC\nsupports up to 3 A, subject to thermal and shared-input limits. Current and\nthermal protection are internal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 141 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5e49e577-2106-4995-bd0f-fa91eca2b12f")
	)
	(text "U1601 (TPS62130A) receives FPGA5V5 at AVIN and both PVIN pins. C1602 (10 uF)\nand C1603 (100 nF) bypass the input. CMD_DDR drives Q1601; a high command\nenables EN_DDR. R1601 (100 kOhm) pulls EN low when Q1601 is off. FPGA5V5 must\nbe available first."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 65.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "60d0c7db-a444-499a-bf30-7a94e5f3dfcf")
	)
	(text "Output and protection"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 136.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6da48d74-d691-49ad-a890-c0e91f26c29a")
	)
	(text "L1601 (2.2 uH) and C1604 (47 uF nominal) filter the switched output. VOS\nsenses DDR_RAW; FSW tied to RAW selects the approximately 1.25 MHz mode as\nRAW rises. Power-save operation is automatic at light load. C1601 (10 nF) on\nSS/TR gives an approximately 5 ms ramp."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 90.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "74f261c4-ebb7-4c16-8690-ed27d356fa8e")
	)
	(text "Output voltage setting"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 111.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8b575961-8c38-465e-9319-15aecb8ca15d")
	)
	(text "Purpose and role"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b716533c-e540-49e9-a2c8-4956914b34d1")
	)
	(text "This converter supplies MIRA's 1.35 V DDR memory domain for data buffering in\nthe FPGA processing path. DDR1V35 also feeds the DDR termination/reference\nsheet, which derives tracking VTT and VREF supplies. Separate control and\nstatus support coordinated startup of memory and its interfaces."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 45.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "db12d34d-0167-465b-b3d6-e6730597b0ec")
	)
	(text "CMD_DDR drives Q1601; R1601 pulls EN low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22 31.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.15 1.15)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 0 70 190 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "de9a0e33-61b8-4892-b32e-db6a26f25840")
	)
	(text "R1603 (11 kOhm) and R1604 (16 kOhm) set the RAW voltage:\nV(DDR_RAW)=0.8 V x (1+R1603/R1604) = 1.35 V.\nTo change it: R1603 = R1604 x (VRAW / 0.8 V - 1). Increasing R1603 raises the\nvoltage. DEF is grounded; the +5% margin is disabled."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 116 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e77576b9-d2df-4908-9350-76d47abd420b")
	)
